{"title":"2006 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 20","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#SOLUTION_NUMBER_2_(Similar_to_the_first_one)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">SOLUTION NUMBER 2 (Similar to the first one)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#SOLUTION_NUMBER_2_(Similar_to_the_first_one)_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">SOLUTION NUMBER 2 (Similar to the first one)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A singles tournament had six players. Each player played every other player only once, with no ties. If Helen won 4 games, Ines won 3 games, Janet won 2 games, Kendra won 2 games and Lara won 2 games, how many games did Monica win?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/d/3ad07ba45d9a4dcd46fbd971320abb2585f7ce0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 0\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 1\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 2\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 3\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"349\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since there are 6 players, a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/d/d2d09b5ba297579ddf128dcc430f58eae639018c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{6(6-1)}{2}=15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"109\" height=\"38\" /> games are played. So far, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/3/d43e6018be8e939b1f4e177905ec8ca91127bb58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4+3+2+2+2=13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"176\" height=\"14\" /> games finished (one person won from each game), so Monica needs to win <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/3/e13073a13501edbec443cf923996f7845ca2b059.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15-13 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ 2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"138\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"SOLUTION_NUMBER_2_.28Similar_to_the_first_one.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"SOLUTION_NUMBER_2_(Similar_to_the_first_one)\">SOLUTION NUMBER 2 (Similar to the first one)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: SOLUTION NUMBER 2 (Similar to the first one)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are six players, so to find the total number of games played, we must do 5+4+3+2+1=15. Next we add 4+3+2+2+2=13. Since, every win represents one game and there are 15 games, Monica has to win 15-13=2 games. So the answer is (c).\n</p><p>-This is by someone\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"SOLUTION_NUMBER_2_.28Similar_to_the_first_one.29_2\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"SOLUTION_NUMBER_2_(Similar_to_the_first_one)_2\">SOLUTION NUMBER 2 (Similar to the first one)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: SOLUTION NUMBER 2 (Similar to the first one)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are six players, so to find the total number of games played, we must do 5+4+3+2+1=15. Next we add 4+3+2+2+2=13. Since, every win represents one game and there are 15 games, Monica has to win 15-13=2 games. So the answer is (c).\n</p><p>-This is by someone.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by WhyMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/M4SEFkUCZ94\">https://youtu.be/M4SEFkUCZ94</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a